<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts bunker prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts bunker prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut the price of its A-888 bunker diesel from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $2 a tonne to $236 effective January 16, the company said.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the Red Sea is $1 lower at $240 a tonne.</p>
<p>From the Gulf, A-960 bunker fuel oil is dropped $5 a tonne to $120 ($18.42 a barrel). From Jeddah and Yanbu A-960 bunker fuel oil is also $5 lower at $124 a tonne ($19.03 a barrel).</p>
</text>
